/accessibility-reports/


# Keep these Yarn PnP files committed:
# .yarn/releases/ (Yarn binary)
# .yarn/sdks/ (IDE integration)
#
# .yarn/cache is deliberately NOT tracked. It could never be complete: next and
# @next-swc exceed GitHub file limits, and the platform-native archives differ
# per OS, so a Windows install deleted the linux ones Vercel builds against.
# Vercel ignores it regardless (vercel.json points YARN_CACHE_FOLDER at
# .next/cache/yarn). yarn install --immutable is what guarantees reproducibility.